    "title": "WWE WrestleMania 42 Card Change: Street Fight Added to Major Match Tonight",
    "text": "WWE adds a Street Fight stipulation to one of tonight’s WrestleMania 42 matches.Apr 19, 2026 4:20 PM EDTJohn Cena speaks to the crowd as host during WrestleMania 42 in Las Vegas.Getty Images WWE has made a late change to the WrestleMania 42 Sunday card. During the WrestleMania Countdown show, Raw General Manager Adam Pearce announced that the scheduled match between Dominik Mysterio and “The Demon” Finn Bálor will now be contested as a Street Fight. The change came after Mysterio, the current AAA Mega Champion, confronted Pearce about being booked against Bálor’s Demon persona, arguing that it was not what he originally agreed to. Pearce acknowledged the complaint before clarifying the situation: Mysterio will still face “The Demon”—but under Street Fight rules, adding a no-disqualification element to the bout. Finn Bálor will wrestle as “The Demon” at WrestleMania 42 in Las Vegas.Getty Images The match will take place tonight at Allegiant Stadium in Las Vegas as part of WrestleMania Sunday, which begins at 6 p.m. ET on ESPN Unlimited. What Other Matches Are Happening Tonight? World Heavyweight Championship: CM Punk (c) vs. Roman ReignsWWE Women’s Championship: Jade Cargill (c) vs. Rhea RipleyUnited States Championship: Sami Zayn (c) vs. Trick WilliamsStreet Fight: “The Demon” Finn Bálor vs. Dominik MysterioIntercontinental Championship — Ladder Match: Penta vs. Rey Mysterio vs. Je’Von Evans vs. Dragon Lee vs. Rusev vs. JD McDonaghSingles Match: Brock Lesnar vs. Oba Femi How Long Is WrestleMania? Night One ran approximately 3.5 hours, and Night Two is expected to follow a similar timeline. The projected end time is between 9:30–10 p.m. ET (8:30–9 p.m. CT / 6:30–7 p.m. PT). A post-show will stream immediately afterward on ESPN Unlimited and WWE’s YouTube channel. You can watch the Countdown show below: Athlon Sports will have full coverage and results of WrestleMania 42 Sunday. More Wrestling NewsThis page may contain affiliate links to legal sports betting or fantasy sports partners. If you sign up, Athlon Sports and The Arena Group may be compensated at no cost to you. Read more about Sports Betting on Athlon Sports.About the authorSteven Harrison is a lifelong WWE fan and experienced writer who brings both creativity and analysis to his work, offering a unique spin on wrestling news and concepts.",
